This project uses [TASKS.md](https://github.com/tasksmd/tasks.md) for agent and human task tracking.

## Format

Tasks live under four priority headings:
```
## P0  — System broken or users blocked. Drop everything.
## P1  — Core work that should ship. Default for planned features.
## P2  — Valuable but not blocking. After P0 and P1 are clear.
## P3  — Someday. Kept for reference, not actively worked.
```

Each task is a Markdown checkbox:
```markdown
- [ ] Short imperative description (@claimant)
  - **ID**: auth-fix
  - **Tags**: backend, auth
  - **Details**: Why the change is needed and what it must accomplish
  - **Acceptance**: Definition of done
  - **Verification**: The runnable command that demonstrates it
  - **Files**: `src/auth/refresh.ts`
  - **Touches**: `src/auth/refresh.ts`, `tests/auth/`
  - **Estimate**: 2h
  - **Risk**: Refactoring the token path — Mitigation: land behind a flag
{% if use_prereg %}
  - **Hypothesis**: Sessions are revoked up to 15 min late because refresh
    tokens outlive access tokens
  - **Success**: P99 revocation latency under 1 s
  - **Pivot**: If latency stays above 5 s, move revocation to the gateway
  - **Measurement**: `uv run pytest tests/auth/test_revocation.py -k latency`
  - **Anchor**: RFC 6749 §1.5, access tokens are bearer and must be short-lived
{{ '' }}{% endif %}
  - **Parent**: auth-overhaul
  - **Surfaced-by**: standing-audit-gap-loop
  - **Blocked by**: other-task-id
  - **Blocked**: needs-user-approval — reason the queue cannot clear
```

`**Acceptance**` is the criterion for done. `**Verification**` is the procedure
that demonstrates it — a command whose exit status decides the question, not a
restatement of the criterion. A task whose Verification cannot be run is not
ready; finish specifying it before starting.

`**Files**` lists everything relevant, including read-only references.
`**Touches**` is the subset the task writes. Two tasks with disjoint `Touches`
sets can run in parallel; overlapping sets conflict and must be sequential.

`**Blocked by**` references other task IDs. `**Blocked**` records a constraint
outside the queue — an approval, a credential, a policy refusal — so a blocked
task is skipped visibly instead of silently.

`**Estimate**` is a rough size (`30m`, `1h`, `2-3d`), used to tell work that fits
one session from work that needs breaking up. `**Risk**` pairs the thing that
could go wrong with how it is contained. `**Parent**` groups a task under a
larger one without making it a sub-task, so it stays separately claimable.
`**Surfaced-by**` records provenance: the audit, sweep, or lint that produced the
task, so a later reader can tell queued findings from requested work.
{% if use_prereg %}
{{ '' }}
Three or more non-trivial tasks in this queue must carry a pre-registration
block of five fields: `**Hypothesis**`, `**Success**`, `**Pivot**`,
`**Measurement**`, and `**Anchor**`. The hypothesis states the prediction, the
success and pivot thresholds make it falsifiable, the measurement is a runnable
command rather than an English description, and the anchor is the source the
threshold came from. Bug fixes are not exempt. Purely mechanical changes are:
their existing CI gate is the metric. If the measurement cannot be run yet, land
the instrumentation first and block the task on it.
{{ '' }}{% endif %}

### Fields agents write, not authors

Three fields exist for work in progress and are managed by whoever claims the
task. Do not pre-fill them; do not hand-edit them on someone else's claim.

- `**Plan**` — a nested checklist of the steps the agent intends to take. It is
  progress state, not a specification, and it is deleted with the task.
- `**Research**` — notes accumulated while investigating, appended under a dated
  subheading. Kept separate from `Details` so a reviewer can tell the author's
  intent from an agent's findings.
- `**Last-enriched**` — the date (`YYYY-MM-DD`) research was last added to a
  blocked task. It gates re-research to once a week per task.

## Rules

- **Completed tasks are removed**, never checked off. Put `closes <task-id>` in
  the commit message so `git log --grep='^closes '` still reports completion.
- **Sub-tasks** use nested `- [x]` checkboxes to track progress. Parent owns all sub-tasks.
- **Promote to separate tasks** when steps can be parallelized or span multiple sessions. Use `**Blocked by**:` for dependencies.
- **Claim tasks** by appending `(@your-name)` before starting work. A claim whose
  agent is gone is stale, not free: ask before taking it.
- **Add new tasks** you discover during implementation — use P2 if unsure of priority.

## Keeping the queue honest

A queue nobody audits fills with work that was never real and misses work that
was never filed. The `standing-audit-gap-loop` task in P2 exists for this: it is
a normal task that asks an agent to audit the repository and **queue findings
rather than fix them**, then delete itself in the same commit. Re-create it
whenever the queue has not been swept in a while.

When every remaining task is blocked, an agent should research rather than idle:
append to `**Research**` under a dated subheading, stamp `**Last-enriched**`,
and leave `**Blocked**` alone. See [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the full protocol.

